# 1. A champion that is in a fight (enemy in basic-attack reach) names that enemy as the team target and raises
#    the call flag in byte 7 (write_shared(7, 1)).
# 2. The flag is cleared (write_shared(7, 0)) only by a champion that sees no enemy champion, so a stale call dies out.
# 3. Hunters, and any healthy farmer, read the flag: when it is raised they walk up to 12 tiles toward the team target
#    (6 tiles otherwise), so fights get joined by 2+ champions instead of 1v1 trades.
# 4. Only when local_strength(8) favours us, so the call does not send weak champions into losing fights.
